WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.400
The best skill your team found is buried in a chat.

2
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:06.800
Skills Board. Your team's skills, all in one place.

3
00:00:06.800 --> 00:00:14.500
Save a skill from its GitHub repository: Skills Board finds the installable skills, and you add the note your team needs.

4
00:00:14.500 --> 00:00:20.500
The recommendation lands in the team library with that note, an example prompt, the source, and the install command.

5
00:00:20.500 --> 00:00:26.200
Teammates search by the task, then narrow by tag: three skills, then two, then the one they need.

6
00:00:26.200 --> 00:00:30.600
Every teammate picks their own handoff: open the source, copy the install command, or download the ZIP.

7
00:00:30.600 --> 00:00:33.700
Group the recommendations into collections the way your team works.

8
00:00:33.700 --> 00:00:41.200
Connected agents read the team library over MCP and get the recommendation, not just a link.

9
00:00:41.200 --> 00:00:45.730
Skills Board, at skillsboard.sh. One place for the skills your team recommends.
